# Build context exclusions.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# The Dockerfile does `COPY configs/ ./configs/`. Docker has no notion of
# `.gitignore`, so without this file that COPY brings `configs/.env` into the
# image -- and a secret copied into a layer is in the image permanently. It
# survives in the layer even if a later step deletes the file, is visible to
# anyone who can pull the image, and is exactly the kind of leak that is
# discovered by a stranger rather than by the person who made it.
#
# The project's `.env` holds live API keys. It is gitignored, and it must be
# dockerignored for the same reason.
#
# Rule for this file: anything that is either (a) a secret, (b) a generated
# artifact, or (c) large and irrelevant to the build, is excluded. When in
# doubt, exclude -- the cost is a rebuild, and the cost of the alternative is a
# leaked key.

# ---- secrets: never in an image -------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
**/credentials.json
overlay.json
**/overlay.json
.secrets/
**/.secrets/

# ---- version control and editor state --------------------------------------
.git
.git/**
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# ---- generated run artifacts ------------------------------------------------
# Results are reproducible from the CLI and are not inputs to a build. They are
# also large, and some of them embed model output.
results/
e2e/
.scratch/
*.pyc
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- agent / local working state --------------------------------------------
.workbuddy-ai/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# ---- documentation and figures -------------------------------------------------
# Not needed to run, and the figures are generated.
docs/
figures/
*.md
!README.md

# ---- local virtualenvs --------------------------------------------------------
venv/
.venv/
env/
node_modules/
